      "id": "6bjaxec",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1.4 Important Banking Terms"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Focus on the establishment (1935) and nationalisation year (1949) of the Reserve Bank of India.",
        "Memorise the major milestones and bank counts during the 1969 and 1980 nationalisation drives.",
        "Be prepared to answer questions on key functions of RBI, monetary policy instruments, and types of bank accounts."
      ],
      "id": "0dwbm1i"
    },
    {
      "id": "crv4u39",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<strong>Current Account + Savings Account deposits as % of total deposits; higher is better for banks: </strong>CASA Ratio",
        "<strong>Loan overdue for more than 90 days; classified as Sub-standard, Doubtful, Loss: </strong>NPA (Non-Performing Asset)",
        "<strong>Capital / Risk-Weighted Assets; minimum 9% under Basel III in India: </strong>Capital Adequacy Ratio (CAR)",
        "<strong>Capital to Risk-weighted Assets Ratio; same as CAR: </strong>CRAR",
        "<strong>Difference between interest income and interest paid; profitability measure: </strong>Net Interest Margin (NIM)",
        "<strong>Gross NPAs / Gross Advances x 100: </strong>Gross NPA Ratio",
        "<strong>Provisions held against NPAs; higher = more buffer: </strong>Provisioning Coverage Ratio",
        "<strong>Banks must lend 40% of ANBC to priority sectors (agriculture, MSME, etc.): </strong>Priority Sector Lending (PSL)"
      ]
    },
